We want to find the value of $N$ such that $(2^3)^{(2^3)} = 2^N$.
Using the property $(a^b)^c = a^{b \cdot c}$, we have
$(2^3)^{(2^3)} = 2^{3 \cdot 2^3}$.
Therefore, $2^N = 2^{3 \cdot 2^3}$.
So $N = 3 \cdot 2^3 = 3 \cdot 8 = 24$.
