completions_13:

\begin{center}
\textbf{Problem:}
If the volume $k_f$ a 2-cm-by-2cm-by-2cm cube is increased by 19 cubic centimeters to form a larger cube, what is the length in centimeters of one edge of the new cube?
\end{center}
Let $s$ be the length of one edge of the original cube.
The volume of the original cube is $V = s^3 = 2^3 = 8$ cubic centimeters.
The volume is increased by 19 cubic centimeters, so the new volume is $V_{new} = 8 + 19 = 27$ cubic centimeters.
Let $x$ be the length of one edge of the new cube. Then the volume of the new cube is $V_{new} = x^3$.
So, $x^3 = 27$.
Taking the cube root of both sides, we get $x = \sqrt[3]{27} = 3$ centimeters.

\boxed{3}
